## Preservation and scope

Accepted earlier targets, failed or interrupted historical evidence, raw operational records, and compressed trace manifests remain preserved. Reversible trace transport changes storage only; decompression must recover the exact receipt-bound original bytes. This review does not authorize removal of historical raw audits or another transport change.

Operational evidence and checker paths may require a privacy-safe public projection. Such a projection must be labelled with its own hash and retain an honest raw-to-public mapping; the raw hashes in this review must not be attached to modified bytes as if they were identical. Mathematical source and audit content remain exact where clean.

This acceptance establishes the stated connected integration and exact trust boundary. It does not prove full practical-solver correspondence, G3 input-only acquisition, general G4 forcing, or broader G6/G7 completion. The source-specific assumptions of the five added modules remain in force.
